 solving and responsibility but hot temper is serious. A has technical but show-off and not open to ideas, also lacking evidence on reliability.\n\nProbably none perfect. Which has least severe concerns? B's nasty remarks could be severe for crew environment. D's hot temper also severe. C's communication difficulty and egocentric also severe. A's show-off and not open to ideas also problematic.\n\nWe might need to ask other agents for missing info, e.g., about reliability of A, stress handling of A, etc. But we need to make a contribution now. Could propose to start with Candidate B because of strong reliability and stress, but note concern about teamwork. Or propose to discuss Candidate B first.\n\nWe need to state current recommendation. Could say I tentatively recommend Candidate B, but need to verify crew cooperation. Or we could hold off and ask for more info.\n\nBut the instruction: \"Your PUBLIC_MESSAGE must: - state or clearly imply your current hiring recommendation\". So we must give a vote now. Choose one.\n\nGiven the data, maybe Candidate B is the best overall despite the nasty remarks, but that is a serious concern. However, reliability and stress are critical for long-distance flights. Could we argue that we can address behavior through training? But the panel should not ignore serious concerns.\n\nMaybe Candidate D has strong problem solving and responsibility, but hot temper is also serious.\n\nCandidate C has calm and quick decisions, but communication issues.\n\nCandidate A has technical but no reliability evidence.\n\nProbably the best overall is Candidate B because reliability and stress are top, and technical competence is decent. The negative behavior is concerning but maybe less impact than hot temper? Both are severe.\n\nI'll vote Candidate B, noting need to address behavior.\n\nThus public message: I propose Candidate B, referencing his conscientiousness, stress handling, weather assessment, but note concern about nasty remarks, and suggest